While fighting a bones ghost unhittable with any
weapon/skill combination my tourist Rnd00077 has, I
got to a wall where a secret door just had to exist,
and started searching for it at the fastest rate
possible while threatened, 1 search per try, typed
fast.

An acid blob "oozed under the door" just as I found
that secret door, but the door, constraining travel
to "straight through", wouldn't let it get past my
PC, standing in front of the doorway.

My eyes not quite keeping up with "see door, see
door replaced by acid blob", I gave whatever was in
the doorway an idle tug, my fingers as usual far
out-running my brain.

Who would have guessed you could o)pen a door with
an acid blob sitting under it?

I hope the acidic blighter got scrape marks all down
his armor-etching back.

